cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the software (this version) and the paper describing it.
type: software
title: "GPU-Native-CFD"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch CUDA reimplementation of two OpenFOAM-family finite-volume solvers (gncHisa, following the
  density-based coupled solver HiSA, and gncRhoSimple, following rhoSimpleFoam) whose whole iteration runs on the
  GPU. In its reference mode every reduction, recurrence and expression is evaluated in the order of the CPU
  original, so that both solvers are bitwise identical to their CPU counterparts over entire runs; a performance
  mode converges to the same discrete solutions. Includes the measurement records behind the accompanying paper.
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Shang-Chih
    affiliation: "Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics, National Cheng Kung University, Tainan, Taiwan"
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - GPU computing
  - CUDA
  - bitwise reproducibility
  - OpenFOAM
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - density-based solver
  - SIMPLE algorithm
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  status: submitted
  title: >-
    Bitwise-reproducible GPU-native rewrites of OpenFOAM solvers: a verification baseline and a comparison of GPU
    porting routes
